 10.1080/01621459.1927.10502953\", \"Direct verified foundational identifier: 10.1080/00401706.1970.10488634\", \"Direct verified foundational identifier: 10.1111/j.2517-6161.1974.tb00994.x\", \"Direct verified foundational identifier: 10.1007/978-0-387-84858-7\", \"Direct verified foundational identifier: 2107.07511\", \"Direct verified foundational identifier: 1905.03222\", \"Direct verified foundational identifier: 1904.06019\", \"Direct verified foundational identifier: 1905.02928\", \"Direct verified foundational identifier: 1903.04684\", \"Direct verified foundational identifier: 1908.08558\", \"Direct verified foundational identifier: 1209.2673\", \"Direct verified foundational identifier: 2202.13415\", \"Direct known JMLR article\"]\nreference collection type: list\n{\n  \"id\": \"ref.Vovk2005\",\n  \"paper_id\": \"10.1007/b106715\",\n  \"citation_key\": \"Vovk2005\",\n  \"title\": \"Algorithmic Learning in a Random World\",\n  \"year\": 2005,\n  \"venue\": \"\",\n  \"query\": \"Direct verified foundational identifier: 10.1007/b106715\",\n  \"source_url\": \"https://api.crossref.org/works/10.1007/b106715\",\n  \"retrieved_at\": \"2026-11-12T23:28:29.761052+00:00\",\n  \"consulted_content\": \"Crossref title, author, venue and abstract fields only; no citation networks accessed; direct DOI OpenAlex abstract, where supplied; direct publisher abstract/description consulted\",\n  \"content_path\": \"literature_evidence/Vovk2005.json\"\n}\ncentral_question \"When does training-only local residual scaling improve the coverage\\u2013reference-mass tradeoff of split-conformal regions for continuous compositions, and what do homoscedastic and covariate-shift controls reveal about its limits?\"\ncentral_thesis \"In the evaluated logistic-normal settings, the frozen training-only scale-selection procedure improves measured coverage\\u2013reference-mass tradeoffs over global ILR calibration under boundary-concentrated heteroscedasticity, provides no consistent homoscedastic advantage, and performs favorably under the tested shift without establishing shifted-distribution validity or a contribution attributable specifically to quantile stumps.\"\nmethod_groups [{\"name\": \"Training-only local scale selection in ILR space\", \"role\": \"proposed\", \"include_reason\": \"The frozen evaluated procedure selects among a quadratic-feature ridge log-scale, a constant, and four ridge/tail log-space blends using three training folds, fitting-only alignment, and a one-standard-error heuristic. Describe and evaluate the entire procedure, not a proven quantile-stump winner.\"}, {\"name\": \"Global ILR split conformal\", \"role\": \"baseline\", \"include_reason\": \"Primary matched comparator: same training-only ridge center, ILR Euclidean residual geometry, calibration split and corrected rank, without covariate-dependent scaling. It isolates scale adaptivity more cleanly than cross-geometry comparisons and is not the original ridge-scale implementation.\"}, {\"name\": \"Raw-simplex L-infinity split conformal\", \"role\": \"baseline\", \"include_reason\": \"Grounded alternative representation and region shape, evaluated on the same target compositions, splits, centers and reference probes. It contextualizes the ILR comparison without claiming geometry is independently ablated.\"}, {\"name\": \"Coordinatewise Bonferroni regions\", \"role\": \"baseline\", \"include_reason\": \"Grounded simultaneous-coordinate comparator using corrected per-coordinate calibration at alpha divided by dimension; expose its coverage and reference-mass tradeoffs rather than reducing comparison to one aggregate score.\"}, {\"name\": \"Constant-scale and permuted-residual controls\", \"role\": \"supporting\", \"include_reason\": \"Training controls examine scale invariance and the dependence on covariate\\u2013residual alignment. Constant scale numerically reproduces global ILR; do not plot it as another independent baseline. Permuted residuals support an alignment interpretation but do not isolate stumps, blend weights, or the selection rule.\"}, {\"name\": \"Calibration and degenerate-region sanity comparators\", \"role\": \"supporting\", \"include_reason\": \"Uncalibrated residual quantiles, the full simplex and a singleton center are available for supplementary checks of coverage\\u2013mass interpretation. They are not competing learned methods and need not dominate the main narrative.\"}]\nnotes_for_writer [\"Draft no paper during strategy generation. This plan is for write-paper-standalone. Later writing, review, audit and revision must independently re-read final.qualification.*; retain any failed qualification and its limitations if the authoritative artifacts change. Here completed/qualified/true is explicit; unspecified diagnostics remain unknown, and no statistical-versus-adaptivity cause should be invented.\", \"Qualification source IDs are final.qualification.status, final.qualification.outcome and final.qualification.correct. Scientific result records are final.evidence.episodes and final.metric.*. The episode grounding entry is a pointer, not an embedded value; follow its json_pointer to the actual episodes. Source-inspected equations and implementation facts additionally require the named local files; do not imply those details were candidate diagnostics verified by the evaluator.\", \"Use ICLR 2026 per VENUE.md, not a newly chosen conference. Inspected .codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/templates/iclr/paper.tex and paper.sty: a single 5.5-inch column, 9-inch text height, normal float width equal to text width. All required figures use preferred_span=full_width meaning that sole text column; no fictitious two-column 0.48-width placement. Keep body between 8 and 9 pages; target 8.5 substantive pages and at least 75% occupancy if ending at 8 pages.\", \"Body allocation including associated floats: abstract/introduction with early overview 1.25 pages; focused related work 0.65; target, geometry, scale procedure and short rank justification 1.85; experimental design, metrics, controls and uncertainty 1.15; condition-structured results with coverage/mass figures and two concise tables 2.40; discussion and limitations 0.95; conclusion 0.25. Total 8.50 pages. Use extra space for the exact reference-measure definition, subgroup contrasts and mechanism caveats, never chronology, repeated tables or generic filler. Keep the main-text limitations and negative H results even if page pressure requires moving detailed pseudocode after references.\", \"Suggested main headings: Introduction; Related Work; Compositional Regions and Training-Only Scale Learning; Evaluation Design; Coverage and Efficiency Across Conditions; Discussion and Limitations; Conclusion. Within results use Homoscedastic Controls, Boundary-Concentrated Heteroscedasticity, and Covariate-Shift Stress Test. These are three conditions of one study, not three discovery stages.\", \"Main Table 1: four-method aggregate utility and decomposed errors/mass, with stored local-minus-comparator paired intervals explicitly aggregate over the fixed six cases. Main Table 2: six-condition local/global/permuted subgroup-error comparison. Do not manufacture cell-specific confidence intervals from the overall paired interval; distinguish descriptive means from stored inferential summaries.\", \"Required quantitative figures must derive every seed point from final.evidence.episodes, export PDF and PNG from the same source with PNG at 300 DPI, and use the PDF in LaTeX whenever available. All full-width raster-only assets must be regenerated at at least 2400 pixels wide, never upscaled; any later column-width-only raster must be at least 1200 pixels wide. At most one overview uses generate-concept-figure; do not create that image in this strategy stage. Preserve editable concept source and provenance later, and record any necessary generator fallback rather than silently changing ownership.\", \"The shared reference distribution is a training-dependent mixture, not invariant simplex volume. Probe-hit Wilson intervals are evaluator-provided binomial-style summaries over clustered query/probe hits; they do not quantify all query-sampling uncertainty. Six seeds and a fixed condition grid limit bootstrap precision and external validity. Do not pool all test examples across seeds as if one independently fitted model generated them.\", \"Do not equate composition-region coverage with class-label prediction-set coverage, calibration of class probabilities, latent multinomial-probability recovery, or true conditional-probability identification. Outputs here are strictly positive continuous logistic-normal responses, not softmax predictions from an evaluated classifier, exact-zero compositions, CIFAR data or finite-count observations.\", \"No recorded component-selection frequency, matched repeated ridge-scale comparison, interaction ablation, sensitivity study or real-data test exists. Neither control success nor a favorable aggregate utility attributes the effect to quantile stumps. The original ridge scale remains a documented component and an untested matched-final comparator, not a demonstrated inferior method.\", \"References and provenance exist, but retrieval metadata alone does not establish relevance or that full text was read. Lei2016DistributionFreePI has a directly relevant title match and is in the allowed starter lineage; verify actual consulted content before citation. Do not fill Related Work with unrelated automatically retrieved entries. Verify suitable ILR, quantile and conditional-coverage context through permitted sources before claiming novelty. Do not identify, search for, open or use the prohibited related paper or citing/discussing pages; stop and record any accidental encounter. This strategy made no network requests.\", \"For double-blind review remove author names, affiliations, acknowledgements, funding and identifying links; do not copy the template's explicit author or final-copy setting. Preserve any required automatically managed watermark block. Include separate LLM Usage after references and any actually required venue checklist; do not invent a checklist requirement from another conference or claim this local style was independently certified as the latest official release.\", \"Supplementary source_ids are registered result anchors for the numerical evidence; implementation, resource and process statements additionally name their actual documentary sources and are not recast as measured findings. Keep the separate mandatory LLM Usage section after references, outside the evidence-backed supplementary subsection array: disclose the evidenced roles in this framing interaction and available proposal, source-editing and reference-query process artifacts, then add the precise writing role when it occurs. Inspect actual logs before attributing additional roles or model versions; do not assert unrecorded manual checks or completed experiments, and record prohibited-literature encounters only if documented. Do not invent a scientific-result source ID for process provenance. This strategy made no network requests. No definitive posthoc analysis ranking is assigned; route the separately authoritative appendix-ranked analyses to Supplementary Information without revising this plan retroactively.\", \"Keep qualitative memory private. Do not use global_memory_summary.md, idea names, or old incomplete status prose to override completed final results. Internal names inside this strategy are private-only grounding instructions, never recommended visible manuscript labels. No final-paper validation, paper.tex, or claims_grounding.json is produced in this stage.\"]\nfinal_evaluation keys: ['correct', 'evaluation_evidence', 'evaluator_sha256', 'manifest_path', 'metrics', 'outcome', 'program_tree_sha256', 'results_tree_sha256', 'status', 'task_tree_sha256']\nfinal metrics: {\"combined_score\": 0.8772268474776957, \"combined_score_ci_high\": 0.878127528